.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
audio/
*.log

# One-off investigation artefacts: scratch transcripts and probe scripts stay
# local, same convention as the scripts/_*.py probes.
episodes/_scratch_*
scripts/_*.py
audio/_*
data/_*
# Review artefacts written at the repo root. ROSTER_DIFF.txt reached a commit before
# this line existed, so name the shape rather than trusting the habit.
*_DIFF.txt
*_diff.txt
# Same: adjudicate_speakers.py's page is regenerated from raw.md in a second, and it
# quotes transcript text the repo already carries.
unresolved_speakers.html
# Video-frame contact sheets and the clip cache behind them (scripts/frames_at.py).
# These are review artefacts, regenerable in seconds, and the cache is video data we
# have no licence to redistribute -- which is the same reason audio/ is ignored.
frames_*.png
ep*-[0-9]*.png
data/frames_cache/
.playwright-mcp/
# Never commit credentials. A `git add -A` once swept scratch logs into this repo,
# so the filenames a key is most likely to land in are blocked by name rather than
# left to discipline. GitHub secret scanning and push protection are the backstop.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*.json
*secret*.json
*token*.json
apikey*
api_key*
.netrc
# Session handoff notes. LOCAL ONLY, owner's decision 2026-09-13: these hold
# point-in-time state ("what is running now", "what needs you"), go stale within hours,
# and tell a public reader nothing about the transcripts. The durable record is
# ARCHITECTURE.md, ENGINEERING_LOG.md, METHODOLOGY.md and CLAUDE.md. Past versions were
# purged from git history with git-filter-repo on the same day.
HANDOFF_*.md
